  "summary": "Malicious code in bigops-timers (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package downloads and executes a remote binary payload. It fetches a payload over HTTPS from three Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev) at /pkg/package (or /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe by platform), with a DNS-TXT-chunked base64 fallback via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded binary is written to /tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe under TEMP on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c \"\u0026\" on Unix). A bundled lib/telemetry.js masquerades as an analytics SDK.",
